[SPEAKER_00]: Because that bad feeling will... might actually make them make proper effort further down the line.

379
00:27:59,048 --> 00:28:02,052
[SPEAKER_00]: If they give in and cover it up and say, no, no, no, it's not about...

380
00:28:02,693 --> 00:28:03,614
[SPEAKER_00]: This is not weakness.

381
00:28:03,754 --> 00:28:04,555
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the strength.

382
00:28:04,575 --> 00:28:04,815
[SPEAKER_00]: What?

383
00:28:04,895 --> 00:28:05,095
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

384
00:28:05,256 --> 00:28:05,616
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not.

385
00:28:05,696 --> 00:28:06,617
[SPEAKER_00]: Strength is giving up.

386
00:28:06,697 --> 00:28:07,518
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not giving up.

387
00:28:08,019 --> 00:28:09,160
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you're not supposed to give up.

388
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,482
[SPEAKER_00]: You're supposed to entertain it.

389
00:28:11,483 --> 00:28:13,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's only a weak person would say that.

390
00:28:13,584 --> 00:28:17,407
[SPEAKER_00]: A person who doesn't know how to give it up, and the only choice for him is to entertain.

391
00:28:17,887 --> 00:28:29,295
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what he ends up doing is basically just, same as before, entertaining sensuality, just kind of developing a different excuse for it, or a more elaborate, or a more meaningful background.

392
00:28:29,315 --> 00:28:31,056
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, I don't know, it's a spiritual practice.

393
00:28:31,877 --> 00:28:33,758
[SPEAKER_00]: Otherwise, because it's just going to be very, very coarse.

394
00:28:33,778 --> 00:28:36,680
[SPEAKER_00]: You're saying that the sense of shame disappears there.

395
00:28:37,406 --> 00:28:38,447
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you would, yeah, yeah.

396
00:28:38,747 --> 00:28:39,887
[SPEAKER_00]: You become stronger than it.

397
00:28:39,907 --> 00:28:40,568
[SPEAKER_00]: You cover it up.

398
00:28:40,788 --> 00:28:46,231
[SPEAKER_00]: You cover the sense of shame when you decide to cover the feeling of guilt for not being able to say no.

399
00:28:47,191 --> 00:28:48,512
[SPEAKER_00]: And your sense of shame goes with it.

400
00:28:49,032 --> 00:28:50,733
[SPEAKER_00]: When you covered it, you covered it up as well.

401
00:28:50,753 --> 00:28:51,274
[SPEAKER_00]: That's progress.

402
00:28:51,574 --> 00:28:51,734
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

403
00:28:52,134 --> 00:28:53,295
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's taken to be progress.

404
00:28:53,315 --> 00:28:54,035
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that's true.

405
00:28:54,255 --> 00:28:54,536
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure.

406
00:28:56,717 --> 00:28:58,998
[SPEAKER_01]: When you're not embarrassed anymore.

407
00:29:00,079 --> 00:29:01,239
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, yeah, there is that practice.

408
00:29:01,259 --> 00:29:01,659
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

409
00:29:01,940 --> 00:29:05,782
[SPEAKER_00]: When you don't feel a sense of shame, doing shameful things.

410
00:29:05,802 --> 00:29:06,002
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

411
00:29:06,748 --> 00:29:20,759
[SPEAKER_00]: But, you know, all this sense of shame, basically, it's not natural, it's the product of society, and you're really going to be empowered if you ignore that it's shameful, and then just go ahead and do it.

412
00:29:20,879 --> 00:29:23,361
[SPEAKER_00]: Nobody should tell you how to live your life.

413
00:29:23,521 --> 00:29:31,708
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is what modern society kind of encourages, one way or the other, because, again, the sense of shame bothers you, the feeling of guilt bothers you.

414
00:29:32,112 --> 00:29:33,272
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you blame others for it.

415
00:29:33,753 --> 00:29:37,494
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't recognize that there is a natural aspect to a sense of shame and feeling of guilt.

416
00:29:38,715 --> 00:29:44,177
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure, if the whole society is repressed, yeah, it's delusional, repressed, whatever else.

417
00:29:44,597 --> 00:29:48,939
[SPEAKER_00]: But, that doesn't mean you should deny the entire sense of shame on a personal level.

418
00:29:49,749 --> 00:29:51,189
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it is quite natural.

419
00:29:51,229 --> 00:29:53,970
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha said, these are the natural protectors of the world.

420
00:29:54,550 --> 00:29:58,811
[SPEAKER_00]: Without a natural sense of shame, well, men would be like dogs.

421
00:29:58,831 --> 00:29:59,491
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

422
00:29:59,671 --> 00:30:04,172
[SPEAKER_00]: Brothers sleep with sisters, sisters with fathers, mothers with sons.

423
00:30:04,272 --> 00:30:08,972
[SPEAKER_00]: Just, just, just, they would be complete, completely serene.

424
00:30:09,592 --> 00:30:12,033
[SPEAKER_00]: But it bothers people.

425
00:30:12,413 --> 00:30:13,533
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't know how to deal with it.

426
00:30:13,773 --> 00:30:17,614
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't have any wisdom in regard to it, to recognize it yet.

427
00:30:17,634 --> 00:30:18,014
[SPEAKER_00]: There is a

428
00:30:19,176 --> 00:30:30,680
[SPEAKER_00]: There is an overflow of, like, shaming and guilt by the society, certain societies in some, I don't know, depressed countries or whatever else, but that doesn't mean that that... that that is the entire thing.

429
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:34,181
[SPEAKER_00]: There is the personal aspect of that sense of shame, because, yeah, it's a shameful thing.

430
00:30:34,401 --> 00:30:35,162
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a private thing.

431
00:30:37,542 --> 00:30:39,123
[SPEAKER_00]: So... and people can't draw that line.

432
00:30:39,263 --> 00:30:39,903
[SPEAKER_00]: They can't see the line.

433
00:30:39,923 --> 00:30:44,445
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when they rebel against it, they rebel against the whole thing, and they become utterly shameless.

434
00:30:47,971 --> 00:30:50,273
[SPEAKER_00]: And you feel liberated.

435
00:30:50,513 --> 00:30:50,854
[SPEAKER_00]: That's it.

436
00:30:50,874 --> 00:30:52,235
[SPEAKER_00]: That's another word people use.

437
00:30:52,275 --> 00:30:53,356
[SPEAKER_00]: Liberated.

438
00:30:53,396 --> 00:30:55,157
[SPEAKER_00]: Because suddenly, you feel free.

439
00:30:55,217 --> 00:31:00,621
[SPEAKER_00]: It's basically like a liberation of... of just giving... opening the floodgates of the desire even more.

440
00:31:01,222 --> 00:31:03,284
[SPEAKER_00]: Or there's... now there's nothing stopping you.

441
00:31:03,704 --> 00:31:05,505
[SPEAKER_00]: Before, you actually had that sense of shame.

442
00:31:06,606 --> 00:31:08,588
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you mistook it to be something that it isn't.

443
00:31:08,708 --> 00:31:09,348
[SPEAKER_00]: You denied it.

444
00:31:09,408 --> 00:31:13,311
[SPEAKER_00]: You made the effort to cover it, to destroy it, to ignore it, to rebel against it.

445
00:31:13,352 --> 00:31:14,232
[SPEAKER_00]: And you feel liberated.

446
00:31:14,272 --> 00:31:16,294
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a liberation of just outpour.

447
00:31:17,732 --> 00:31:26,378
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, sure, it feels a relief when you open the gates, but you wouldn't feel a relief if you were to know where these floods are taking you.

448
00:31:27,059 --> 00:31:30,421
[SPEAKER_00]: If they're taking you down the messy waterfall, you're gonna crash at the bottom.

449
00:31:30,962 --> 00:31:33,063
[SPEAKER_00]: You will not feel a relief if somebody opens the gate.

450
00:31:33,303 --> 00:31:35,745
[SPEAKER_00]: You will feel life-threatening.

451
00:31:35,865 --> 00:31:43,491
[SPEAKER_00]: And on the contrary, you would feel relieved if the gates could stay closed, so you don't flow down the waterfall where you're gonna crash into death.

452
00:31:44,698 --> 00:31:50,783
[SPEAKER_00]: But not knowing that, yeah, oh, yeah, it's a joyous ride until, oh, it's too late now to swing back.

453
00:31:50,923 --> 00:32:05,916
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there's one approach trying to escape such things, sensuality, is to take tantric, is tantric Buddhism, tantric, you know... Ah, it's a contradiction in terms.

454
00:32:05,956 --> 00:32:06,236
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

455
00:32:06,256 --> 00:32:07,637
[SPEAKER_00]: Contradictions.

456
00:32:07,657 --> 00:32:09,299
[SPEAKER_01]: And meditation.

457
00:32:09,399 --> 00:32:10,360
[SPEAKER_00]: Sexual celibacy.

458
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:11,801
[SPEAKER_00]: Tantric Buddhism.

459
00:32:14,260 --> 00:32:24,328
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, Buddha, he goes on to encourage celibacy, brahmacharya, and there's a sutta on that, where he describes what that is.

460
00:32:24,368 --> 00:32:30,493
[SPEAKER_01]: And some would say this is the other extreme, like complete suppression of all these desires.

461
00:32:30,513 --> 00:32:32,634
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, it's just not this restrictive.

462
00:32:32,674 --> 00:32:32,915
[SPEAKER_01]: It is.

463
00:32:33,515 --> 00:32:34,016
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely.

464
00:32:34,036 --> 00:32:34,896
[SPEAKER_00]: You're beating yourself up.

465
00:32:34,916 --> 00:32:42,162
[SPEAKER_00]: You suppress the desires because you see them pointless, meaningless, insatiable, and only result in harm.

466
00:32:43,772 --> 00:32:45,773
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, by all means, suppress it.

467
00:32:46,793 --> 00:32:49,254
[SPEAKER_00]: Because through that suppression, wisdom might arise.

468
00:32:50,414 --> 00:32:54,776
[SPEAKER_00]: One thing for sure, wisdom will not arise from giving in.

469
00:32:54,796 --> 00:32:59,237
[SPEAKER_00]: So, wisdom will not necessarily arise through somebody who is practicing full-on restraint.

470
00:33:01,038 --> 00:33:04,479
[SPEAKER_00]: So, wisdom will not necessarily arise just from that, but it can.

471
00:33:05,317 --> 00:33:08,860
[SPEAKER_00]: And one thing for sure, it cannot arise if there is no basis of restraint.

472
00:33:09,240 --> 00:33:29,015
[SPEAKER_00]: That's another sutra where it says, even if somebody spends their whole life without, kind of, developing any wisdom, just through sheer restraint and saying no to desires, and even if they go through extreme pains because of that, and spend their whole life in tears for the rest of their life, it's still much better than giving in, like, just once.

473
00:33:29,836 --> 00:33:32,738
[SPEAKER_00]: Because in the long run, again, you spend years

474
00:33:33,700 --> 00:33:39,330
[SPEAKER_00]: Forcefully, for somebody with no wisdom, keeping the mind away from giving into centrality.

475
00:33:39,831 --> 00:33:41,293
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's making lots of merit.

476
00:33:43,157 --> 00:33:44,800
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, you know, people think merit...

477
00:33:46,545 --> 00:33:48,046
[SPEAKER_00]: For the future life, it's just through giving.

478
00:33:48,086 --> 00:33:49,727
[SPEAKER_00]: No, that was the lowest aspect.

479
00:33:49,967 --> 00:33:54,849
[SPEAKER_00]: When I said, yeah, through giving, through giving to one person, to Mopa, to the Buddha, to Arahant, to Saṅgha, you get more.

480
00:33:55,149 --> 00:34:06,355
[SPEAKER_00]: But none of that would equal the amount of merit, the streams of merit you would make, like if you develop a finger snap of a right view, a finger snap of freedom from sensuality.

481
00:34:06,375 --> 00:34:06,935
[SPEAKER_00]: Non-cruelty.

482
00:34:06,995 --> 00:34:08,356
[SPEAKER_00]: A finger snap of non-cruelty.

483
00:34:08,396 --> 00:34:09,456
[SPEAKER_00]: Finger snap of loving-kind.

484
00:34:09,536 --> 00:34:10,397
[SPEAKER_00]: A finger snap.

485
00:34:11,077 --> 00:34:14,559
[SPEAKER_00]: So, somebody for a whole lifetime... That's what I meant when I said in the beginning.

486
00:34:14,579 --> 00:34:15,360
[SPEAKER_00]: It's actually...

487
00:34:15,420 --> 00:34:20,804
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if somebody doesn't want to be an arahant or whatever, it would be much better if they would practice celibacy.

488
00:34:22,125 --> 00:34:29,910
[SPEAKER_00]: If they would say no to sexual desire, the mind would already grow by itself just through that, let alone if they make extra effort to gain wisdom.

489
00:34:31,773 --> 00:34:34,874
[SPEAKER_00]: Even if it's painful for the rest of your life, so what?

490
00:34:35,534 --> 00:34:37,314
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just, what, measly 50-60 years.

491
00:34:37,694 --> 00:34:39,455
[SPEAKER_00]: How many years have you been reborn?

492
00:34:39,495 --> 00:34:41,935
[SPEAKER_00]: How many years you will be reborn on account of that?

493
00:34:42,496 --> 00:34:46,236
[SPEAKER_00]: 50 years of crying your eyes out because of the pain of restraint?

494
00:34:46,777 --> 00:34:47,137
[SPEAKER_00]: Nothing.

495
00:34:47,197 --> 00:34:48,217
[SPEAKER_00]: They will go up in smoke.

496
00:34:48,297 --> 00:34:48,737
[SPEAKER_00]: No time.

497
00:34:51,438 --> 00:34:53,998
[SPEAKER_01]: The pain of restraint or the fever of sensuality?

498
00:34:54,338 --> 00:34:55,078
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

499
00:34:55,619 --> 00:34:57,519
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, that's like, you know,

500
00:34:58,263 --> 00:35:07,526
[SPEAKER_00]: The most, the many you can imagine, just practicing sensual restraint, non-cruelty towards people, non-entertaining yourself, not your desires, for the rest of your life.

501
00:35:08,687 --> 00:35:10,247
[SPEAKER_01]: But what about...

502
00:35:10,587 --> 00:35:14,889
[SPEAKER_00]: Eons of heavenly rebirth, because those are the mental states, they will take you there.

503
00:35:17,830 --> 00:35:23,292
[SPEAKER_01]: But maybe I'm... if I have children, giving them opportunity to... to hear the dhamma.

504
00:35:25,339 --> 00:35:26,299
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I don't follow that.

505
00:35:26,319 --> 00:35:26,519
[SPEAKER_01]: What?

506
00:35:26,579 --> 00:35:28,400
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, people have children they want to give.

507
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:33,582
[SPEAKER_01]: I've heard it before, that you want to give other beings... Ah, no, sorry.

508
00:35:33,622 --> 00:35:39,024
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they had children in order for those children to later have opportunity to get dharma.

509
00:35:39,044 --> 00:35:39,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

510
00:35:40,465 --> 00:35:43,786
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that sounds... sounds like a terrible excuse.

511
00:35:50,047 --> 00:35:54,171
[SPEAKER_00]: How about... because there is no guarantee you're going to become an arahant, even if you hear the dhamma.

512
00:35:54,392 --> 00:36:00,979
[SPEAKER_00]: So, hearing the dhamma in itself can be quite meaningless, if a person doesn't know how to attend to it, or doesn't want to.

513
00:36:01,980 --> 00:36:08,887
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, you can say to those people who want to have children, in order for children to hear the dhamma, maybe, it would be better if they become arahants themselves.

514
00:36:09,648 --> 00:36:11,610
[SPEAKER_00]: So, instead of, eh...

515
00:36:12,979 --> 00:36:21,665
[SPEAKER_00]: Optional, a remote possibility of somebody becoming an arahant by hearing the dhamma in the future, they can become arahants themselves and learn one lesson saṃsara.

516
00:36:22,465 --> 00:36:23,526
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the most you can do.

517
00:36:26,388 --> 00:36:30,611
[SPEAKER_00]: But obviously, that is much harder to do that than to produce a child.

518
00:37:00,821 --> 00:37:03,804
[SPEAKER_01]: So go and read the sutra on celibacy.

519
00:37:09,079 --> 00:37:22,532
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then a brahmin, Janasoni, approached the Blessed One and exchanged greetings with Him and said to Him, Does Master Gautama also claim to be one who lives the celibate life?

520
00:37:24,122 --> 00:37:35,025
[SPEAKER_01]: And the Buddha replies, if Brahman one could rightly say of anyone, he lives the complete and pure celibate life, unbroken, flawless, unblemished, unstained.

521
00:37:35,045 --> 00:37:37,206
[SPEAKER_01]: It is precisely of me that one might say this.

522
00:37:37,866 --> 00:37:43,868
[SPEAKER_01]: For I live the complete and pure celibate life, unbroken, flawless, unblemished, unstained.

523
00:37:45,569 --> 00:37:50,150
[SPEAKER_01]: But what, Master Gautama, is a breach, flaw, a blemish and a stain of the celibate life?

524
00:37:54,531 --> 00:38:06,417
[SPEAKER_01]: It's here a Brahmin, some ascetic or Brahmin, claiming to be perfectly celibate, does not actually engage in intercourse, sexual intercourse with a woman, but he consents to being rubbed, massaged, bathed.

525
00:38:07,795 --> 00:38:08,556
[SPEAKER_01]: Good point, yeah.

526
00:38:36,157 --> 00:38:49,320
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, some ascetic or brahmana, claiming to be perfectly celibate, does not actually engage in intercourse with women, does not... nor does he consent to being rubbed, massaged, but he jokes with women, plays with them and amuses himself with them.

527
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:56,080
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, he does not joke with women, play with them, and amuse himself with them, but he gazes and stares straight into their eyes.

528
00:38:57,120 --> 00:39:02,301
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, he does not gaze and stare straight into the woman's eyes, but he listens to their voices behind a wall.

529
00:39:03,882 --> 00:39:06,703
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, through a rampart, as they laugh, talk, sing, or weep.

530
00:39:07,763 --> 00:39:16,906
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, he does not listen to their voices, voices of women behind a wall, but he recollects laughing, talking, and playing with them in the past.

531
00:39:18,719 --> 00:39:29,107
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, he does not recollect laughing, talking and playing with them in the past, but he looks at a householder enjoying himself furnished and endowed with five objects of sensual pleasure.

532
00:39:31,311 --> 00:39:54,139
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, he does not look at a householder, enjoying himself furnished and endowed with five objects of sensual pleasure, but he lives the spiritual life, aspiring for rebirth in a certain order of devas, thinking, by this virtuous behavior, observance, and austerity, or spiritual life, I will be a deva, or one in the retinue of the devas.

533
00:39:54,659 --> 00:39:58,921
[SPEAKER_01]: He relishes this desire, and desires it, and finds satisfaction in it.

534
00:39:59,661 --> 00:40:03,803
[SPEAKER_01]: This, too, is a breach, a flaw, a blemish and a stain of the celibate life.

535
00:40:04,683 --> 00:40:06,424
[SPEAKER_00]: Of the perfect celibate life, can't it?

536
00:40:07,004 --> 00:40:07,464
[SPEAKER_00]: Perfect, yeah.

537
00:40:07,924 --> 00:40:11,966
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, the reason why I say that is because... Now, people might think, oh, human, I must not do anything.

538
00:40:12,346 --> 00:40:19,409
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's actually better to at least be virtuous, even if you are desiring for the sake of rebirth, than to be engaging in sexuality.

539
00:40:19,909 --> 00:40:22,350
[SPEAKER_00]: Because there's that sort of a venerable nānda,

540
00:40:23,273 --> 00:40:25,014
[SPEAKER_00]: was struggling and wanted to disrobe.

541
00:40:25,834 --> 00:40:27,916
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha said, why do you want to disrobe?

542
00:40:27,936 --> 00:40:32,078
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, well, there was this servant girl, that was quite pretty, and she told me, when I come back, she'll be waiting for me.

543
00:40:33,132 --> 00:40:37,456
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he said... and then he showed him that the beauty... the Buddha showed him the beauty of the devas.

544
00:40:37,776 --> 00:40:40,859
[SPEAKER_00]: There's 500 nymphs or whatever it was in the suttas.

545
00:40:41,600 --> 00:40:43,281
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he said, well, which is prettier?

546
00:40:43,441 --> 00:40:45,243
[SPEAKER_00]: The nymphs or that servant girl?

547
00:40:45,423 --> 00:40:46,884
[SPEAKER_00]: And he said, well, the nymphs.

548
00:40:46,964 --> 00:40:49,446
[SPEAKER_00]: The servant girl is like a... Cauterized monkey.

549
00:40:49,466 --> 00:40:51,608
[SPEAKER_00]: Cauterized monkey with the ears burned off.

550
00:40:51,628 --> 00:40:52,749
[SPEAKER_00]: It's nothing in comparison.

551
00:40:52,769 --> 00:40:56,212
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, okay, well, I can guarantee you, you're gonna have

552
00:40:57,033 --> 00:41:02,995
[SPEAKER_00]: Those anims, they were anims, if you practice celibacy for the rest of your life, that will be your rebirth.

553
00:41:03,656 --> 00:41:05,516
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he was like, okay, well, I'll do that then.

554
00:41:05,557 --> 00:41:06,497
[SPEAKER_00]: Then you got motivation.

555
00:41:06,957 --> 00:41:13,680
[SPEAKER_00]: However, sometime later, the monks heard that and then they were basically looking down upon him and he felt ashamed.

556
00:41:13,700 --> 00:41:16,421
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he actually made the effort properly and became an arahant.

557
00:41:16,901 --> 00:41:19,442
[SPEAKER_00]: But yeah, it is better, even if you're designing heaven.

558
00:41:20,423 --> 00:41:26,425
